---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import Brand from '../components/Brand.astro';
import CtaButtons from '../components/CtaButtons.astro';
import StatBar from '../components/StatBar.astro';
import HeroVisual from '../components/HeroVisual.astro';
import CreatorGrid from '../components/CreatorGrid.astro';
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';
import FinalCta from '../components/FinalCta.astro';
import { TIERS, CTA, PROOF, PENDING, estherMonths } from '../data/site';
import { HOME_FAQS, HOME_COMPARE } from '../data/content';
import { faqPage, person, services } from '../data/schema';
const months = estherMonths();
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Creator Seeding for Beauty Brands · Influencer Orbit"
  description="Beauty influencer marketing agency: 50 to 150+ real creator posts a month for US skincare brands, guaranteed by day 60. Done for you."
  path="/"
  schema={[faqPage(HOME_FAQS), person(), ...services()]}
>
  <!-- 1. Hero -->
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="container hero__inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">The creator seeding operation for beauty brands</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title" class="display-hero">We help US skincare and beauty brands get 50 to 150+ real creator posts every month, <em>guaranteed by day&nbsp;60</em>, without hiring an influencer team.</h1>
      <p class="lead">With the Orbit Seeding Engine, every creator confirms before a single unit ships. You approve a brief and ship from your own warehouse. We find, vet, confirm and follow up until every post is live.</p>
      <CtaButtons micro="See the live tracker and a real monthly report before you commit to anything." />
    </div>
    <div class="container">
      <HeroVisual />
      <div class="hero__proof">
        <img src="/images/brand/esther-formula-logo.webp" width="869" height="96" alt="Esther Formula" />
        <span>Seeding partner since {PROOF.estherSince} · {PROOF.totalPosts} creator posts live</span>
        <span class="hero__platforms" role="img" aria-label="Platforms: Instagram, TikTok, YouTube"><Brand name="instagram" decorative /><Brand name="tiktok" decorative /><Brand name="youtube" decorative /></span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2. Proof bar -->
  <div class="container stats-wrap"><StatBar /></div>

  <!-- 3. Problem -->
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="problem-title">
    <div class="container split split--top">
      <div>
        <h2 id="problem-title" class="display-lg">You didn’t build a skincare brand to chase creators who never post.</h2>
        <figure class="post-rate">
          <figcaption class="post-rate__title">Posts you get back from every 100 boxes shipped</figcaption>
          <div class="post-rate__row">
            <div class="post-rate__label"><span>Cold gifting</span><b>30 to 50</b></div>
            <div class="post-rate__track"><i class="post-rate__range" style="left:30%;width:20%"></i><i class="post-rate__fill post-rate__fill--muted" style="width:30%"></i></div>
          </div>
          <div class="post-rate__row">
            <div class="post-rate__label"><span>Confirm-first, Influencer Orbit</span><b class="is-us">70+</b></div>
            <div class="post-rate__track"><i class="post-rate__fill" style="width:70%"></i></div>
          </div>
          <div class="post-rate__boxes" aria-hidden="true">
            {Array.from({ length: 20 }).map((_, i) => <span class={i < 14 ? 'on' : ''}></span>)}
          </div>
          <p class="post-rate__note">Cold gifting range: <a href="https://blog.hypeauditor.com/how-to-get-influencers-to-post-about-your-brand-during-a-gifting-campaign/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">HypeAuditor</a>. Confirm-first: Influencer Orbit program data.</p>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="pull">Most creator programs don’t fail because of the wrong creators or the wrong strategy. They fail on operations: boxes ship, nobody follows up, and half the product never turns into a post.</p>
        <p>You search your brand on TikTok and find almost nothing. Then you search a competitor with a weaker formula and scroll through dozens of real faces talking about them.</p>
        <p>You’ve tried. Eight hours a week of DMs. Boxes that shipped three weeks ago with nothing to show for it. Maybe a coordinator who is now at capacity, or an agency that sent your product to the wrong creators.</p>
        <p>Cold gifting programs see only 30% to 50% of creators actually post (<a href="https://blog.hypeauditor.com/how-to-get-influencers-to-post-about-your-brand-during-a-gifting-campaign/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">HypeAuditor</a>). Meanwhile US Meta prices per ad rose 23% year over year in Q3 2026, and your ad creative burns out every few weeks with nothing behind it.</p>
        <div class="callout">
          <strong>The problem isn’t creator seeding. It’s running it by hand, or capping it at what one person can manage.</strong>
          <p>That’s where we come in. Influencer Orbit takes founder-led beauty brands from 5 to 15 scattered posts a month to 50 to 150+ confirmed creator posts, using the Orbit Seeding Engine. It’s built for founders who want the channel to run without them and judge it in cost per post, not impressions.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4. Definition (answer block) -->
  <section class="section--tight" aria-labelledby="def-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="definition reveal">
        <h2 id="def-title">What is product seeding?</h2>
        <p class="prose">Product seeding is sending your product, free, to hand-picked creators so they post about it in their own words. Done at volume, it builds social proof, TikTok search presence and a steady supply of ad-ready UGC for far less than paid placements. The hard part is operations: finding, vetting, confirming, shipping and following up with every creator.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5. How it works -->
  <section class="section" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="how-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head section-head--center">
        <h2 id="how-title" class="display-lg">The Orbit Seeding Engine runs in four steps.</h2>
        <p class="lead">One rule runs through all of them: no creator gets product until they confirm. That single change is why 70%+ of our creators post, against 30% to 50% for cold gifting.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li class="step reveal">
          <div class="step__top"><span class="icon-tile"><Icon name="scan-search" /></span><span class="step__when">Days 1–5</span></div>
          <h3>Competitor Creator Audit</h3>
          <p>We map which creators already post for three of your direct competitors, which hooks get the most views, and which formats win in your category. That becomes your brief and outreach scripts, approved by you. Outreach goes live by day 5.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step reveal">
          <div class="step__top"><span class="icon-tile"><Icon name="user-check" /></span><span class="step__when">Days 5–21</span></div>
          <h3>Confirm-first seeding</h3>
          <p>We hand-vet creators for audience fit, engagement quality and content match, not follower count. Every creator confirms before your warehouse ships anything. You get confirmed addresses daily.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step reveal">
          <div class="step__top"><span class="icon-tile"><Icon name="circle-play" /></span><span class="step__when">Day 21 on</span></div>
          <h3>Posts live and tracked</h3>
          <p>Posts go live and we chase every one until it shows in your live tracker. You see every creator, shipment and post link in real time.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step reveal">
          <div class="step__top"><span class="icon-tile"><Icon name="zap" /></span><span class="step__when">Day 30 on</span></div>
          <h3>Amplify and report</h3>
          <p>Your best posts become Spark Ads, and top performers join your VIP Creator Roster for repeat seeding and paid collabs. Your first monthly report lands on day 30.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <div class="center-note">
        <p class="muted">Each step removes a reason seeding programs stall: wrong creators, ghosted boxes, and good posts that never become ads.</p>
        <p><a class="text-link" href="/creator-seeding">See the full process and pricing <Icon name="arrow-right" /></a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 6. Who it's for -->
  <section class="section section--white" aria-labelledby="fit-title">
    <div class="container fit-layout">
      <div class="fit-intro">
        <h2 id="fit-title" class="display-lg">Built for founders who think in <em>cost per post</em>.</h2>
        <p class="lead">We work best with Shopify-native brands doing $500K to $10M a year, with 2 to 50 people, who can approve a brief in 48 hours and ship within three business days.</p>
        <dl class="icp" aria-label="Ideal client profile">
          <div><dt><Icon name="badge-dollar-sign" />Revenue</dt><dd>$500K–$10M a year</dd></div>
          <div><dt><Icon name="users" />Team</dt><dd>2 to 50 people</dd></div>
          <div><dt><Icon name="globe" />Market</dt><dd>US DTC beauty</dd></div>
          <div><dt><Icon name="store" />Store</dt><dd>Shopify-native</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div class="fit-board">
        <div class="fit-board__col">
          <h3>This is for you if you run a US DTC skincare, cosmetics or beauty brand and you:</h3>
          <ul class="fit">
            <li><Icon name="circle-check" /><span>Want your brand showing up when shoppers search your product or hero ingredient on TikTok</span></li>
            <li><Icon name="circle-check" /><span>Gift product now but get 5 to 15 posts a month, or have plateaued at what one coordinator can handle</span></li>
            <li><Icon name="circle-check" /><span>Are tired of boxes that vanish, agencies that report “estimated reach”, and ad creative that dies every three weeks</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="fit-board__col fit-board__col--no">
          <h3>The wrong fit if</h3>
          <ul class="fit fit--no">
            <li><Icon name="circle-x" /><span>Your warehouse can’t ship within three business days of creator confirmations</span></li>
            <li><Icon name="circle-x" /><span>You can’t approve briefs within 48 hours</span></li>
            <li><Icon name="circle-x" /><span>You need a guarantee on views or sales rather than posts</span></li>
            <li><Icon name="circle-x" /><span>You’re outside US skincare, cosmetics or beauty</span></li>
          </ul>
          <p class="fit-board__note">We’ll tell you on the call, not after you’ve paid.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="situations">
        <div class="situation">
          <span class="icon-tile"><Icon name="clock" /></span>
          <div><h3>If you’re running seeding yourself</h3><p>You get 10x the volume back without adding headcount, and your 8 hours a week back.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="situation">
          <span class="icon-tile"><Icon name="handshake" /></span>
          <div><h3>If you already have a coordinator</h3><p>We import your roster and tracker and work alongside your current setup. Volume grows. It never restarts.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="center-cta"><CtaButtons /></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 7. Proof -->
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="proof-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="proof-card reveal">
        <div>
          <h2 id="proof-title" class="display-lg"><span data-months>{months}</span> months. Same client. Here’s what that looks like.</h2>
          <img class="proof-card__logo mt-8" src="/images/brand/esther-formula-logo.webp" width="869" height="96" alt="Esther Formula" loading="lazy" />
          <p>We’ve run the creator seeding operation for Esther Formula, a Korean skincare and beauty supplement brand, since January 2024.</p>
          <ul class="checks">
            <li><Icon name="check" /><span>2,000+ creator collaborations and {PROOF.totalPosts} creator posts live</span></li>
            <li><Icon name="check" /><span>70%+ post rate under confirm-first, against 30% to 50% for cold gifting</span></li>
            <li><Icon name="check" /><span>50 to 200 creator posts live every month, for <span data-months>{months}</span> months straight</span></li>
            <li><Icon name="check" /><span>200+ product shipments coordinated every month, with no in-house influencer manager ever hired</span></li>
          </ul>
          {PENDING.estherTestimonial && (
            <blockquote class="testimonial"><p>“{PENDING.estherTestimonial.quote}”</p><footer class="mt-4 small">— {PENDING.estherTestimonial.name}, {PENDING.estherTestimonial.title}, Esther Formula</footer></blockquote>
          )}
          <p class="mt-6"><a class="text-link" href="/case-studies">Read the full case studies <Icon name="arrow-right" /></a></p>
        </div>
        <CreatorGrid count={9} />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 8. Pricing preview -->
  <section class="section section--white" aria-labelledby="price-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head section-head--center">
        <h2 id="price-title" class="display-lg">Priced per program. Measured per post.</h2>
        <p class="lead">One offer in three tiers, from $1,500 a month. Every tier starts with a 60-day pilot, then runs month to month.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tiers">
        {TIERS.map((t) => (
          <article class={`tier${t.popular ? ' tier--popular' : ''}`}>
            {t.popular && <span class="tier__badge">Most popular</span>}
            <h3>{t.name}</h3>
            <p class="tier__price">${t.price.toLocaleString('en-US')}<span> / month</span></p>
            <p class="tier__posts"><strong>{t.posts.split(',')[0]}</strong> creator posts a month</p>
            <p class="tier__meta">Management cost {t.perPost} per post</p>
            <p>{t.bestFor}</p>
            <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="/creator-seeding#pricing">See what’s included</a>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 9. Guarantee -->
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="guarantee-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="guarantee reveal">
        <p class="guarantee__label"><Icon name="shield-check" />The guarantee</p>
        <h2 id="guarantee-title" class="display-lg">Your post count, live by day&nbsp;60. <em>In writing.</em></h2>
        <p>Pick your tier. If your tier’s monthly post count isn’t live by day 60, month three is free and we keep working with no management fee until it is. You keep every creator contact, every content link and the tracker, whether you stay or not.</p>
        <p class="fine">We guarantee posts, not views. Posting is what we control. The algorithm isn’t.</p>
        <div class="mt-8"><CtaButtons dark micro={false} secondary={false} /></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 10. Comparison -->
  <section class="section section--white" aria-labelledby="compare-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head section-head--center">
        <h2 id="compare-title" class="display-lg">Influencer Orbit vs. an in&#8209;house hire vs. a typical agency</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="compare-title">
        <table class="data-table">
          <thead><tr><th scope="col"><span class="sr-only">Feature</span></th>{HOME_COMPARE.cols.map((c, i) => <th scope="col" class={i === 0 ? 'is-us' : ''}>{c}</th>)}</tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {HOME_COMPARE.rows.map(([label, ...cells]) => (
              <tr><th scope="row">{label}</th>{cells.map((c, i) => <td class={i === 0 ? 'is-us' : ''}>{c}</td>)}</tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="table-note center">In-house cost is a US influencer marketing coordinator’s salary before software. Full comparison, including software and marketplaces, on the <a href="/creator-seeding#compare">Seeding Engine page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 11. Founder -->
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="founder-title">
    <div class="container founder">
      <div class="founder__photo">
        <picture>
          <source type="image/avif" srcset="/images/brand/tayyab-habib-480.avif 480w, /images/brand/tayyab-habib-800.avif 800w" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 380px, 90vw" />
          <img src="/images/brand/tayyab-habib-800.webp" srcset="/images/brand/tayyab-habib-480.webp 480w, /images/brand/tayyab-habib-800.webp 800w" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 380px, 90vw" width="800" height="800" alt="Tayyab Habib, founder of Influencer Orbit" loading="lazy" />
        </picture>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <h2 id="founder-title" class="display-lg">Hi, I’m Tayyab, founder of Influencer Orbit.</h2>
        <p class="mt-6">After running influencer work for 100+ brands, I noticed the same thing in almost every gifting program: product went out, half the creators never posted, and nobody followed up.</p>
        <p>That’s why we built the Orbit Seeding Engine, a confirm-first seeding operation with one job: real creator posts, every month, at volume.</p>
        <p>We’ve run it for the same beauty brand for <span data-months>{months}</span> months, across 2,000+ creator collaborations. I care about one number more than any other: posts against target.</p>
        <p class="founder__sign">Tayyab Habib</p>
        <a class="btn btn--primary mt-6" href="/book" data-cta="founder"><Icon name="calendar" />Want to work together? Book a call.</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 12. FAQ -->
  <section class="section section--white" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head section-head--center">
        <h2 id="faq-title" class="display-lg">Questions founders ask before booking</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-center"><Faq items={HOME_FAQS} /></div>
      <p class="center-note"><a class="text-link" href="/creator-seeding#faq">More answers on the Seeding Engine page <Icon name="arrow-right" /></a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 13. Final CTA -->
  <FinalCta
    title="Ready to see 100+ creator posts go live next month?"
    text="Let’s talk. In 20 minutes we’ll show you the live Esther Formula tracker and the exact monthly report you’d receive. Then we’ll run the cost-per-post math against what you spend now."
    secondary={false}
    micro='Not ready for a call? <a href="/competitor-audit">Get your free Competitor Creator Audit</a> and see which creators already post for your top 3 competitors.'
  />
</BaseLayout>
